y the Soviet-led boycott. The 1983 World Champion had been Finland’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/67499"} "Tiina Lillak"] ", who had won in front of her home country fans. Two British throwers, " [:a {:href "/athletes/68811"} "Fatima Whitbread"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/68770"} "Tessa Sanderson"] ", were also among the world’s top javelinists. Whitbread was the runner-up in 1983 at Helsinki, while the bronze medalist at the Worlds was another woman competing in Los Angeles, " [:a {:href "/athletes/70697"} "Anna Verouli"] " of Greece, who had also won the 1982 European Championships. In round one, Sanderson took the lead with 69.56 (228-2¾) and that would hold up for the gold medal. Lillak recorded 69.00 (226-4½) in the second round despite a foot injury that caused her to pass her last four throws, but that was good enough for silver."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Qualifying"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "172"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/68770"} "Tessa Sanderson"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} "61.58 (5)"] [:td {} "69.56 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "Olympic Record"} "OR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "97"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/67499"} "Tiina Lillak"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FIN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FIN.png"}] "FIN"]] [:td {} "63.30 (2)"] [:td {} "69.00 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:clas